{
 "about": "Distance of each of the four configurations from the unquantized BF16 model, on two reference sets that hold BF16 outputs (RESULTS.md section 12). KL in nats; 0 is identical, lower is closer. Descriptive: no gate and no ranking rule; every interval computed is listed and none was selected. The two sets use different measures and are not comparable with each other. Neither reaches past 14.4K: the 64K and 127K lengths of the task runs have no BF16 reference here. Differences b - a: negative means b is closer to BF16. The three probe arms share their K4 experts, so a difference between two of them reflects the tensors outside the experts. exlr8-k4 is a different checkpoint from the three probe arms, not a setting of the same one. Any difference from a probe arm is a whole-checkpoint difference and is not attributable to one component. anchor is the reference of the probe, not a recommendation.",
